# Script Style Guide (Luau)

Follow these defaults in this repository unless a file already uses a different established pattern.

- Keep code simple and readable; prefer short single-purpose functions.
- Match project patterns over novel abstractions when uncertain.

## Naming

- Public/main functions: `PascalCase` (example: `ShowRevealVFX`)
- Private/helper functions: `_camelCase` (example: `_refreshCounters`)
- Local variables: `camelCase`
- Module tables and types: `PascalCase`
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`

## File Order

Use this order in most Luau scripts:
1) pragma (`--!strict`), 2) optional short purpose comment, 3) Services, 4) requires, 5) Constants, 6) Types, 7) private state, 8) private helpers, 9) public API, 10) `return ModuleTable`.

## Function + Comment Style

- Prefer action-oriented names (`Show...`, `Play...`, `Bind...`, `Refresh...`).
- Prefer early returns over deep nesting.
- Keep comments short and intent-focused; avoid obvious comments.
- Use short `--[[ ... ]]` doc blocks for public functions or non-obvious helpers.
- In doc blocks, describe params in gameplay/system terms, not just types.

## Controller/UI/Data Practices

- Keep controller update loops centralized when possible.
- Use explicit `BindToRenderStep` names and explicit unbind/cleanup.
- Validate payloads at boundaries; keep schema/runtime keys consistent.
- Use explicit fallback values for missing/invalid data.
- Return safely (with guarded fallbacks) for non-critical visual failures.
